    "passage": "A lucky charm is something which is thought to bring good luck. Certain objects are believed to have the ability to [[1]] such positive spiritual energy. One of the most-well known [[2]] of good fortune is a horseshoe. It is said that a horseshoe hanging over the door protects and brings good fortune for the family [[3]] inside.\nDo you know why horseshoes became lucky charms? One explanation is that they [[4]] blacksmiths whose jobs were considered very lucky. Since early Western Europeans believed that iron and fire would [[5]] evil spirits, blacksmiths were thought to have special powers, such as the ability to heal the sick. Their work with horses also brought them much respect. Not only because they made lucky horseshoes but also they protect the safety of the horsemen.",
